Quick Recap of Kahn’s Algorithm
Purpose: Performs Topological Sorting of a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG)
Idea:
Find all nodes with in-degree = 0 (no dependencies)
Insert them into a queue
Remove one node from the queue, add it to output
Reduce in-degree of its neighbors by 1
If any neighbor’s in-degree becomes 0 → put it in queue
Repeat until queue empty
Real-Life Example Scenario
Project Task Scheduling

Imagine you’re managing a construction project:

Tasks & Dependencies:
Task ID	Task Name	Depends On
1	Lay foundation	None
2	Build walls	1
3	Install roof	2
4	Paint walls	2
5	Install windows	2
6	Final inspection	3, 4, 5
Dependency Graph
This forms a DAG:

